<p>The war involving Iran has sharply disrupted shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, a key chokepoint for energy and other commodities. The shock is rippling well beyond the Middle East. Asian economies that rely heavily on oil and liquefied natural gas moving through the strait have rushed to manage supply risks, as tanker traffic slows to a near standstill and officials warn it’s still unclear when routes will normalize. In South Asia, shortages of liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) used for cooking are starting to disrupt daily life and small businesses, with rationing and long lines reported in parts of the region. The disruption is also reaching agriculture: with Gulf output constrained and gas prices rising, fertilizer supplies have tightened and prices have climbed, adding to worries about knock-on pressure on food costs.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/SfNOBH5UVULTPJMT7nxqAlJBDf3dPEwCTjaX6VboP9b3lPmJbe7TK42LfiB9pA1gUIJOYZjrbNzhxexsHoAyfEE2MT82a3GIOHRs6-CRmKkEpDXd_lCPIjKDAZB1cdUOe5Dam2iVGUVfz6B_odHDg6-TA8oqdgsjyRumDlz3rvt2bm2bpgpc' alt='Signs reading &#x27;out of stock&#x27; at a gas station amid rising petrol prices in Manila, Philippines on March 9, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Workplace adjustments: Vietnam’s Ministry of Industry and Trade urged employers to allow remote work where possible, as the energy shock begins to affect everyday routines.</li><li>Fuel import exposure: Bangladesh imports nearly 95% of its energy needs, a vulnerability now in sharper focus as prices rise and rationing, panic buying, and long lines set in.</li><li>Potential tanker measures: Asian officials said the US could ease market pressure by enlisting other countries to help guarantee insurance for tankers transiting Hormuz. They added they have not seen signs of such steps yet.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Washington-based Asia diplomat: A Washington-based Asia diplomat said, “We’re not receiving any communication from the Trump administration,” and said the best outcome would be an end to the conflict. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/11/asia-oil-crisis-trump-iran-war-00824189'>Politico</a>)</li><li>India restaurants sector: Restaurants across India warned they may have to close within days because of LPG shortages. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/11/2026/energy-crisis-disrupts-south-asia'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/war-disrupts-fertiliser-supplies-puts-food-security-risk'>War disrupts fertiliser supplies, puts food security at risk</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/india/634505-lpg-imports-india-bangladesh-pakistan/'>‘This is going to hit all of us’: How far does the echo of the Middle East war reach?</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/11/asia-oil-crisis-trump-iran-war-00824189'>America’s Asian allies scramble to address oil crisis with little guidance from Trump</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/un-warns-global-aid-at-risk-as-middle-east-war-spreads'>UN warns of risk to global aid as Middle East war spreads</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://restofworld.org/2026/asia-remote-work-gulf-war-energy-crisis-lpg/'>The Gulf war is reshaping how Asia works</a> - restofworld.org</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/11/2026/energy-crisis-disrupts-south-asia'>Energy crisis disrupts South Asia</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/12/asia-energy-crisis-iran-war'>Asia scrambles to confront energy crisis unleashed by Iran war – with no end in sight</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>